      "blocks": {
        "question-1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is the cooking surface really titanium, or a titanium coating?",
            "answer": "<p>Titanium. The LavaCell™ surface is a solid titanium layer bonded into the pan's body — not a spray, a paint or a \"titanium-reinforced\" non-stick coating. There is nothing applied on top of it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What does \"5-ply\" mean?",
            "answer": "<p>Five metal layers bonded into one body: titanium at the surface, then a titanium shield, a triple aluminium thermal core, an 18/10 stainless steel structure and an 18/0 magnetic stainless base. Each does one job; together they behave as a single sheet of metal.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does a surface release food without a coating?",
            "answer": "<p>The hexagonal relief holds a micro-film of oil in its valleys, while the raised peaks reduce the area food can grip. Combined with a properly preheated pan, proteins form a crust and release on their own.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why aluminium in the middle?",
            "answer": "<p>Aluminium conducts heat more than ten times better than stainless steel. Three layers of it pull heat from the burner out to the rim quickly and evenly, so the whole base cooks — not just the centre.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-5": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can the layers separate over time?",
            "answer": "<p>They're forged and bonded under pressure, not glued, and built to stay as one. Delamination under household use is covered by the lifetime warranty.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question-6": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why is the pan safe at 260°C when coated pans aren't?",
            "answer": "<p>There is no polymer to soften or break down. Titanium and stainless steel are stable far beyond any oven temperature; 260°C is the limit we rate for the handle and the whole assembly.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
